.TH geectl-local-build-precommit 1  "geectl-local-build-precommit 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-local\-build\-precommit \- The precommit gate: the `precommit`\-mode service run, then `pre_checkin.sh` when the source directory carries one
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl local\-build precommit\fR [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDIRECTORY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
The precommit gate: the `precommit`\-mode service run, then `pre_checkin.sh` when the source directory carries one.
.PP
The script step is part of the gate, not of the service mode: the mode filter alone runs services only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The OBS project the services validate against: in a git checkout it names the parent project, in an OBS checkout it defaults to the checkout\*(Aqs project, and a value that disagrees with the checkout refuses
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR \fI<TIMEOUT_SECS>\fR [default: 3600]
Timeout in seconds for the whole gate
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIDIRECTORY\fR>
The source directory carrying the `_service` file and optionally `pre_checkin.sh`
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
